@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<div class="container py-5">

    <!-- Page Header -->

    <div class="text-center mb-5">

        <h1>
            Privacy Policy
        </h1>

        <p class="lead">
            How information is handled by this system
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- Introduction -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            1. Introduction
        </h2>

        <p>
            This website is a student-developed disaster relief
            management system created for academic and educational
            purposes.
        </p>

        <p>
            The system has been designed to demonstrate how a web
            application can support the management of relief projects,
            volunteers, employees, donors and donations.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-info mt-4">

            <strong>Academic Project Notice:</strong>

            This website is not the official Gift of the Givers
            website and is not operated by Gift of the Givers.

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- Information Collected -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            2. Information Collected
        </h2>

        <p>
            Depending on which features of the system are used,
            the application may collect information submitted by
            users through its forms.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4">
            Donor Information
        </h3>

        <p>
            Registered donors may provide information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>First name and surname</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Contact number</li>
            <li>Physical address</li>
            <li>Donation information</li>
            <li>Donation frequency</li>
            <li>Donation amount</li>
            <li>Donation currency</li>
            <li>Selected fund option</li>
        </ul>


        <h3 class="mt-4">
            Volunteer Information
        </h3>

        <p>
            Volunteers may provide information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Name and surname</li>
            <li>Contact information</li>
            <li>Address</li>
            <li>Volunteer discipline</li>
            <li>Professional registration information where applicable</li>
            <li>Next of kin information</li>
            <li>Availability</li>
            <li>Geographic deployment preferences</li>
            <li>Additional information about skills and experience</li>
        </ul>


        <h3 class="mt-4">
            Contact Information
        </h3>

        <p>
            Users who submit the contact form may provide their
            name, email address, subject and message.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Account Information -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            3. User Accounts
        </h2>

        <p>
            The system uses authentication to manage access to
            protected features.
        </p>

        <p>
            Registered users may be required to provide an email
            address and password when creating or accessing an
            account.
        </p>

        <p>
            Passwords are handled using the application's
            authentication framework rather than being stored
            as plain-text passwords.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Anonymous Donations -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            4. Anonymous Donations
        </h2>

        <p>
            The system provides an option for a user to make a
            donation without creating or using a registered donor
            account.
        </p>

        <p>
            Anonymous donation refers to the donor not being
            associated with a registered donor account within the
            application. Donation information required by the
            system may still be recorded for demonstration and
            administrative purposes.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- How Information Is Used -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            5. How Information Is Used
        </h2>

        <p>
            Information submitted to the system is used to
            demonstrate and support the application's intended
            functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
            This may include:
        </p>

        <ul>

            <li>
                Managing donor accounts and donations
            </li>

            <li>
                Managing volunteer applications and availability
            </li>

            <li>
                Supporting relief project management
            </li>

            <li>
                Providing employee access to project information
            </li>

            <li>
                Generating donation records and placeholder
                tax certificates
            </li>

            <li>
                Demonstrating authentication and authorisation
                functionality
            </li>

        </ul>

    </section>


    <!-- Donations -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            6. Donations and Payments
        </h2>

        <p>
            This application is an academic prototype.
        </p>

        <p>
            Donation amounts, currencies and donation records are
            used to demonstrate the functionality of the system.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-warning mt-4">

            <strong>Important:</strong>

            This prototype does not process real financial
            transactions or transfer money to Gift of the Givers.

        </div>

        <p>
            Any tax certificate generated by the prototype is a
            placeholder document created for demonstration
            purposes and should not be treated as an official
            tax certificate.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Data Security -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            7. Data Security
        </h2>

        <p>
            The application uses authentication and authorisation
            mechanisms to help restrict access to protected
            functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
            Access to employee functionality is restricted to
            authenticated users assigned the appropriate employee
            role.
        </p>

        <p>
            Security features implemented within the application
            are intended to demonstrate appropriate software
            development practices for an academic project.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Employee Access -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            8. Employee Access
        </h2>

        <p>
            Authorised employees can access protected areas of
            the system to perform functions such as managing
            relief project information, posting project updates
            and viewing volunteer sign-ups.
        </p>

        <p>
            Employee access is controlled through role-based
            authorisation.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Data Sharing -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            9. Sharing of Information
        </h2>

        <p>
            This academic prototype is not intended to sell,
            rent or commercially distribute information submitted
            through the application.
        </p>

        <p>
            Information within the system is intended to support
            the demonstration of the application's functionality
            and database design.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Cookies -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            10. Cookies and Technical Data
        </h2>

        <p>
            The application may use cookies or similar technical
            mechanisms required by the web framework to support
            authentication, sessions and normal website
            functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
            These technologies are used to support the operation
            of the application rather than for advertising or
            commercial tracking.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- External Links -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            11. External Websites
        </h2>

        <p>
            The website may contain references or links to external
            websites. External websites operate independently and
            may have their own privacy policies and terms.
        </p>

        <p>
            Users should review the privacy policies of external
            websites before providing them with personal
            information.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Changes -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            12. Changes to This Privacy Policy
        </h2>

        <p>
            This privacy policy may be updated as the academic
            project develops and additional functionality is
            implemented.
        </p>

        <p>
            Any changes will be reflected on this page.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- Contact -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2>
            13. Contact
        </h2>

        <p>
            If you have questions about this academic prototype
            or how the system handles information, please use
            the contact functionality provided on the website.
        </p>

        <a asp-page="/Contact"
           class="btn btn-primary mt-2">

            Contact Us

        </a>

    </section>


    <!-- Final Academic Notice -->

    <div class="alert alert-info mt-5">

        <strong>Academic Project:</strong>

        This Privacy Policy describes the intended information
        handling practices of a student-developed prototype.
        It does not represent the official privacy policy of
        Gift of the Givers.

    </div>

</div>
